-Only sound/motion settings, best score, and last seed are stored locally. There are no campaign saves, accounts, telemetry, external assets, or network services. Unknown profile versions remain untouched. Future profile changes require a migration and fixture update.
+Game results use 24 alternating drives plus sudden-death overtime, not a snap-level football engine. Player totals are distributed from team production. There is no on-field player control, detailed playbook, draft-pick trading, multi-player trades, negotiation market, relocation, broadcast radio, preseason exhibition schedule, or coach hiring carousel. The schedule rotation uses fixed within-division pairing slots for its two extra conference games rather than prior-year placement. Playoff tiebreakers use win percentage, point differential, points scored, then stable team ID. These are explicit first-release simplifications.
 
